bbmp: StSound takes sizes and counts from the file and reads where they say (the final
audit of 7 October 2026): a short or damaged YM or Digi-Mix (MIX1) file made it read past
the file and crash. Every read of the loader now stays inside the file (a damaged file is
refused); the LZH unpacker refuses code tables a damaged file makes impossible; the player
keeps a tracker note, a YM 2 drum and a loop point inside what the song has. Real songs
play byte for byte as before.
